# 13. CLOUDINARY FILE MANAGEMENT AND COMPRESSION

Build a centralized file upload service.

Supported files:
- Profile photos.
- Company logos.
- Company banners.
- Candidate resumes.
- Optional job-related documents.

PDF requirements:
- All PDFs must be less than 1 MB before being stored in Cloudinary.
- Validate MIME type and PDF signature.
- Apply PDF compression before upload.
- Verify compressed output size.
- Reject files that remain 1 MB or larger.
- Avoid unnecessary repeated compression.
- Store secure Cloudinary URLs and public IDs.
- Delete replaced files when safe to do so.
- Prevent public exposure of sensitive candidate documents.

Image requirements:
- Compress images.
- Resize profile images.
- Generate optimized formats such as WebP/AVIF when supported.
- Use responsive image delivery.
- Avoid oversized uploads.

Use secure backend upload endpoints and environment-based Cloudinary credentials.

Do not store file binaries in MongoDB.

